{
  "_comment": [
    "The cryptod service definition and the machine's crypto policy keys.",
    "",
    "Identity is Service, cryptod's own virtual account. That's not",
    "optional: libpcrypto trusts a policy copy only if SYSTEM or cryptod's",
    "service SID owns it, and a file cryptod creates is owned by its token's",
    "user. Under LocalService every process would refuse the policy and fall",
    "back to Peios's defaults. cryptod logs an error if it finds itself",
    "running as anything else.",
    "",
    "RequiredPrivileges are SeChangeNotifyPrivilege, to traverse, and",
    "SeAuditPrivilege, to write its events; cryptod-policy.reg grants them",
    "to cryptod's service SID. No SeTcbPrivilege: cryptod queues its records",
    "under KMES's per-process rate instead.",
    "",
    "ExecStartPre runs prepare-state as SYSTEM (HookIdentity) to create",
    "/var/state/cryptod, where cryptod keeps the policy across reboots for",
    "processes that start before it. peinit provisions /run/<service> and",
    "nothing else, and /var/state is SYSTEM's, as timed-service.reg explains.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): cryptod notifies once it has published the",
    "policy and is listening for reports. A process that starts first reads",
    "the copy kept across reboots, so nothing need be ordered after cryptod.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2): while cryptod is down, policy changes",
    "aren't published and reports are lost. ErrorControl is Normal (0):",
    "processes keep using the last policy published, so the machine is",
    "usable without it.",
    "",
    "The Cryptography key is created here with Peios's defaults explicit,",
    "agreed on PEI-1721, so that they're visible to anyone reading the",
    "registry. cryptod applies the same defaults if the key is absent:",
    "  Reject MinimumGrade = U   refuse only the floor",
    "  Warn MinimumGrade = C     record the use of anything graded U or D",
    "  FIPS = 0 for both         approval doesn't matter",
    "  Exceptions Enabled = 1, AllowExceptionsToReject = 1,",
    "  WarnByDefault = 0, WarnAlways = 0",
    "Packages add exceptions under Exceptions\\<Owner.Purpose> in .reg",
    "files of their own. The key inherits the hive root's descriptor:",
    "SYSTEM and Administrators may change it, every authenticated user,",
    "cryptod among them, may read and watch it.",
    "",
    "Shipped into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an image names it in",
    "[registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\cryptod",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/cryptod" },
        { "name": "Triggers", "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "Service" },
        {
          "name": "RequiredPrivileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["SeChangeNotifyPrivilege", "SeAuditPrivilege"]
        },
        {
          "name": "ExecStartPre",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["/usr/libexec/cryptod/prepare-state"]
        },
        { "name": "HookIdentity", "type": "sz", "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["cryptod"] },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Crypto policy" },
        {
          "name": "Description",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Publishes the machine's crypto policy and records the weak cryptography in use"
        }
      ]
    },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Cryptography" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Cryptography\\Reject",
      "values": [
        { "name": "MinimumGrade", "type": "sz", "data": "U" },
        { "name": "FIPS", "type": "dword", "data": 0 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Cryptography\\Warn",
      "values": [
        { "name": "MinimumGrade", "type": "sz", "data": "C" },
        { "name": "FIPS", "type": "dword", "data": 0 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Cryptography\\Exceptions",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Enabled", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "WarnByDefault", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "WarnAlways", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "AllowExceptionsToReject", "type": "dword", "data": 1 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
